(7173305, 1099583, 23098, '<td valign="top">Congrats!  Super shot.</td>', 'Congrats!  Super shot.', '2014-02-08 22:54:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(7173563, 1099872, 30861, '<td valign="top">This garnered a 9 from me, exquisitely balanced layering-up of nuances here.</td>', 'This garnered a 9 from me, exquisitely balanced layering-up of nuances here.', '2014-02-09 19:55:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7175218, 1099598, 109387, '<td valign="top">Cool! I was searching for other people using a go pro and I find out that your image had been taken with that camera!<br/> <br/>I''ve seen the time lapse too. Have you used a motorized slider? It''s awesome how the Go Pro worked on the scene without flickering - have you edited the images a lot or the camera simply did a super job?</td>', 'Cool! I was searching for other people using a go pro and I find out that your image had been taken with that camera! I''ve seen the time lapse too. Have you used a motorized slider? It''s awesome how the Go Pro worked on the scene without flickering - have you edited the images a lot or the camera simply did a super job?', '2014-02-12 09:19:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7176519, 1099601, 74979, '<td valign="top">Nicely done.. what a beautiful image. Much depth and great variation in color and textures.<br/> <br/>the sky is amazing isn''t it?  a perpetual subject..<br/> <br/>edited to add.. you know Brad, what I find most appealing about many of your images is that for the most past, you present the "real" of what you captured.. you get the concept of the "equivalent" as put forward by Alfred Stieglitz.  The HDR craze makes me nuts.. if it''s not good enough as nature presents it, what''s the point?  I know there''s some "clean up" which must be done in the digital world to make an image its best.  Purist is an artform.  but I suspect you already know this.<br/> <br/>A<br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2014-02-14 10:43:23.</i></td>', 'Nicely done.. what a beautiful image. Much depth and great variation in color and textures. the sky is amazing isn''t it?  a perpetual subject.. edited to add.. you know Brad, what I find most appealing about many of your images is that for the most past, you present the "real" of what you captured.. you get the concept of the "equivalent" as put forward by Alfred Stieglitz.  The HDR craze makes me nuts.. if it''s not good enough as nature presents it, what''s the point?  I know there''s some "clean up" which must be done in the digital world to make an image its best.  Purist is an artform.  but I suspect you already know this. A ', '2014-02-14 10:35:07.000000', '2014-02-14 10:43:23.000000', 0),
